How to run the gate: push the branch, `gh workflow run checks.yml --repo avra-lang/avra --ref <branch>`
(needs hd-gate's "a hand-dispatched run climbs its branch's rungs too" commit), then
`gh run view <id> --log-failed`.

Found by s-gate (in every gate since 41422086942, unlisted): #15 std-avrac/@features-a: `features/node_print — the language's own nodes` traps `unwrapped an absent value` (node_print_test.av:181): `avra().wordings` has no `Expr.Range` (loops' bare `counted = lo ".." hi` and ranges' parenthesised rule read differently, so "one node, one surface" drops it) and no `Pat.Wild` (five rules build it). Owner: hd-nodes. FIXED cb752647: a loop head's range and a pattern's `..` are `by` computed builders (core/computed.av), so each node keeps one wording; green in gate 41439910381.

## #12 / #13 triage (gate 41439910381, hd-gate cb752647; s-gate)
cache-attacks (a): 11 failed of 519 steps. cache-attacks (b2): store-clean 4 failed of 17. Messages are the script's own first line. Owners are by mechanism read from the case, not confirmed by the owner.

| case | first message | owner |
