Unowned: none. The `ur`/`us` rows are the least certain: a warm check that printed no `Q parse` line at all could be a held entry (hold) or the trace line's moved spelling (decl); s-hold should check the trace first.

abx re-opened by gate 41446148140: AB wanted `held N/M` in the output, and a comment edit is now answered by the verdict (`cache cache hit`, ea06d1b2). AB accepts a cache hit as a hold (hd-gate, after 48704c95).
